      "nets": ["NET0032", "NET0022", "NET0046", "NET0042", "NET0028"],
      "observed": "Five keyboard column outputs are connected to SKW92A pins identified in the netlist as Ethernet PHY signals: COL1 to LAN_PORT1_TX+, COL2 to LAN_PORT1_TX-, COL3 to LAN_PORT1_RX+, COL4 to LAN_PORT1_RX-, and COL5 to LAN_PORT2_RX+.",
      "expected": "The specification says the keyboard's five column and seven row lines are wired to SKW92A GPIO pins for matrix scanning. The keyboard columns should not be connected to Ethernet PHY signal pins.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"NET0032\") ... (ref \"U10\") (pin \"7\") (pinfunction \"COL1\") ... (ref \"U6\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"LAN_PORT1_TX+\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"NET0022\") ... (ref \"U10\") (pin \"9\") (pinfunction \"COL2\") ... (ref \"U6\") (pin \"6\") (pinfunction \"LAN_PORT1_TX-\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"NET0046\") ... (ref \"U10\") (pin \"10\") (pinfunction \"COL3\") ... (ref \"U6\") (pin \"7\") (pinfunction \"LAN_PORT1_RX+\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"NET0042\") ... (ref \"U10\") (pin \"17\") (pinfunction \"COL4\") ... (ref \"U6\") (pin \"8\") (pinfunction \"LAN_PORT1_RX-\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"NET0028\") ... (ref \"U10\") (pin \"19\") (pinfunction \"COL5\") ... (ref \"U6\") (pin \"9\") (pinfunction \"LAN_PORT2_RX+\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "netlist shows 5 column + 7 row lines wired directly to SKW92A GPIO pins (matrix scanned by the module itself)"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The keyboard scan signals are placed on Ethernet PHY lines rather than GPIOs. This can prevent reliable keyboard scanning and interfere with, or electrically stress, the PHY signals.",
      "confidence": 0.87
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The keyboard column nets connect directly to SKW92A pins designated as Ethernet PHY signals, contradicting the specified GPIO matrix wiring. This is a functional connectivity deviation; the documented unconnected RJ45 is not counted separately."
}

